## What the schema cannot hold

- **No SIN in any form.** `ExtractionBoxValue` refuses the SIN box at
  construction, so no box row can carry one; `ExtractionCorrectionRecord`
  refuses a correction naming that box; `CorrectionField` has no Box 12 member.
  A planted `123456789` reaches no column and no read shape.
- **No address column.** An address is persisted only as an opaque correction
  value the closed field vocabulary identifies — never in an audit row, never in
  a dedicated column. `PiiSchemaTests`' `Address` fragment ban holds.
- **No source reference and no content key.** The key that reaches the encrypted
  source object stays in the intake metadata that already holds it, so no query,
  index, or diagnostic here can reach content. No `byte[]` column exists.
- **No token, claim, presence, prompt, payload, fingerprint, or file name**
  column, and no free text in any audit row: every audit column is a closed enum
  value, an opaque identifier, a sequence, or an instant.
- **No tax year.** No extraction table declares a `TaxYear` column, a tax-year
  check constraint, or a year authority of any kind.
- Every enum is stored as an integer; the currency is `CurrencyIsKnown` plus
  `CurrencyCodeAsPrinted`, two explicit scalar columns rather than a converted
  complex value; the medical date and amount are stored as printed text.
- Every row carries the exclusive seven-year `RetentionUntilUtc` the **existing**
  `RetentionPolicy` computes. No second retention authority is declared.

## Append-only and firm-scoped

Every store member appends. The contract declares no update, delete, upsert,
save, replace, or purge member, and the implementation issues no `Update`,
`Remove`, `ExecuteUpdate`, or `ExecuteDelete` call. A second version leaves the
prior row byte-unchanged; a re-appended version number loses on the primary key
and commits nothing partial; a duplicate resolution leaves its determination row
untouched and a second decision on one candidate is refused by the database.

Every member takes a `TrustedFirmId` first with no omitting overload, and every
member is additionally case-scoped. A foreign-firm read and a missing row are
both `null`; a foreign-firm write is `NotFound` and stores nothing.

## The eight authorized downstream guards

Three stay **closed, additive registration only**:

- `tests/Persistence.Tests/Boundaries/PersistenceBoundaryTests.cs` — adds
  `ExtractionWorkflow` to the exact reference set, and registers the new
  migration designer file in the approved tax-year-literal inventory, because a
  designer snapshot re-emits the whole model including the existing
  `[TaxYear] = 2025` intake constraint. That registration authorizes nothing
  further: no extraction production file contains a tax-year literal.
- `tests/Persistence.Tests/Schema/MigrationTests.cs` — adds exactly the one new
  migration to the ordered inventory.
- `tests/Persistence.Tests/Schema/ModelShapeTests.cs` — adds the ten entities to
  `ExpectedEntityTypes`; the inventory stays explicit and closed and the
  exactly-one-dedicated-configuration assertion is intact.

Four are **opened without losing their guarantee**, each mutation-checked:

- `tests/Persistence.Tests/Upgrade/EfUpgradeBaselineTests.cs` — the comparison is
  now scoped by the tables the stored spec 013 baseline itself records, not by a
  `.Intake` name filter that spec 015 would have had to extend. Every baseline
  table, column, key, index, and relationship is still compared byte-for-byte.
  *Mutation: shortening a baseline column and separately renaming a baseline
  table each fail it.*
- `tests/TaxAI.Portal.Tests/Upgrade/UpgradeBaselineContractTests.cs` — the exact
  post-baseline reference set and type-prefix set become individually reviewable
  lists naming `ExtractionWorkflow` and the extraction namespaces. Baseline
  signatures, friend assemblies, embedded resources, migration bytes, and floors
  are untouched. *Mutation: an unapproved project reference and an unapproved
  internal type each fail it.*
- `tests/ExtractionWorkflow.Tests/BoundaryTests.cs` — the exact total file
  inventory becomes a required set: each T02 and T03 file exists exactly once at
  its approved path. *Mutation: moving `IExtractionStore.cs` fails it.*
- `tests/ExtractionWorkflow.Tests/Models/ResultShapeTests.cs` — the exact total
  public-type inventory becomes rule-based sweeps over every public type: sealed
  class, never a record, hand-written `ToString()`, no post-construction
  mutation, no mutable collection, no raw-byte or stream carrier outside the
  lease, factories hiding invariant-bearing constructors. *Mutation: a settable
  property and a `byte[]` property each fail it.*

Two of the eight — `RepositoryVerificationTests.cs` and the three Persistence
guards above — needed only the one-line registration each.

## Not in this task, and absent from the tree

No ingest workflow, `DocumentExtractionIngress`, medical validator, duplicate
detector, or projection (T04). No review workflow, correction, override, or
acceptance path (T05). No HTTP route, component, content-reader implementation,
or composition-root wiring beyond the one store registration (T06). No
verification record (T07).

No provider invocation, no review-record creation, no case acceptance workflow,
no retention or purge path, and no deployment authorization. The spec 011
deployment refusal, the spec 012 review route, the twelve spec 014 intake
routes, the two existing migrations, and every existing public contract are
unchanged.

